{"type":"text","timestamp":1794528699091,"sessionID":"ses_e2dc43e6affebafhf3YG0vzqkm","part":{"id":"prt_1d23ed88a002QAfxAyf0TbVN4I","sessionID":"ses_e2dc43e6affebafhf3YG0vzqkm","messageID":"msg_1d23ec018001RnVMmyHtpHdIY5","type":"text","text":"T017 implemented and verified.\n\n**Files written**\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`\n  - `newTally` and `tallyBlock` carry `cappedStartRows`.\n  - `addScored` now counts only uncapped start rows in `startRows`/`started`, and capped start rows in `cappedStartRows`.\n  - The text arm line prints `capped start rows <n>`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`\n  - Added one summary case with a capped start row (`exit: 143`) and an uncapped start row (`exit: 0`), expecting `startRate: '1 of 1'` and `cappedStartRows: 1`.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  47 passed (47)\n```\n\n```\n$ node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '.opencode.pre | {startRate, cappedStartRows}'\n{\"startRate\":\"2 of 7\",\"cappedStartRows\":5}\n```\n\n7 + 5 = 12, the arm's start-row count. Also ran `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`: exit 0.\n\n**Could not do**\n\n`$SP/summary-before.json` does not exist on disk (it is T001's output, and no copy exists anywhere in the repo). To check the verify condition I captured `$S --summary $PRE --json` immediately before editing: `.opencode.pre.startRate` was `\"5 of 12\"`, so the arm holds 12 start rows. The post-change 7 + 5 equals that 12. I did not recreate the missing T001 artifact, since it is outside this task's named files. `tasks.md` was not touched and T017 remains unticked.","time":{"start":1794528696458,"end":1794528699091}}}
